Foods to Keep Handy When Your Period Starts

Having a few simple foods at home can make period days easier. You do not need to buy special products. Keeping versatile ingredients in your kitchen can help you prepare quick meals when you do not feel like spending a lot of time cooking.

Bananas are convenient because they require no preparation and can be eaten as a snack. They can also be added to oatmeal, smoothies, yoghurt, or toast.

Oats are another useful pantry staple. They can be prepared as sweet oatmeal with fruit or as savoury oats with vegetables and spices.

Lentils and beans are valuable pantry ingredients because they can provide protein, fibre, and minerals. They can be used to prepare dal, curries, soups, salads, and simple one-pot meals.

Nuts and seeds can be kept ready for snacks. Almonds, peanuts, walnuts, pumpkin seeds, and sunflower seeds can be added to breakfast or eaten in small portions between meals.

Frozen vegetables can be useful when fresh vegetables are not available. They can be added to rice dishes, curries, soups, noodles, or omelettes.

Yoghurt can be another convenient food. Eat it with meals, combine it with fruit, or use it as a base for a simple snack.

Seasonal fruits can also be kept available. Choose affordable options that your family enjoys rather than feeling that you need expensive specialty foods.

You can prepare some meals in advance too. A batch of dal, vegetable soup, or khichdi can make meal preparation easier on days when you want to rest.

While checking your kitchen supplies, remember your period-care products too. Keep enough sanitary pads at home and consider storing a few in your handbag, backpack, or travel pouch.

A small period-care kit can contain sanitary pads, tissues, and any other personal essentials you normally use. Having everything together makes it easier to grab when you are leaving home.

When selecting sanitary pads, consider comfort, absorbency, fit, and your normal menstrual flow. Personal preferences can vary, so choose what works for you.

